WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.100
In the year 499, an Indian astronomer
called Aryabhata wrote that the earth turns

2
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:07.560
on its axis.

3
00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.970
The Bhagavad Gita pictures
whole worlds that dawn,

4
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.680
fade into night, and dawn again.

5
00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:18.500
Indian doctors had already written
great textbooks of medicine and surgery.

6
00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.630
So does modern science fit
Hindu belief, or clash with it?

7
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.620
In this mission, you'll meet ancient
Indian astronomy and medicine,

8
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.800
and an old school of thought that
sorted matter into principles.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:35.330
Then you'll set those vast cycles
of time beside the Big Bang.

10
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:40.280
Your mission: find out how Hindus have
answered the challenge of modern science.
